+
+**Numbered Steps:**
+1. Initialize `entry = 0`.
+2. Compare start parameters to find the largest:
+   - If `tx0` is the largest (`tx0 > ty0` and `tx0 > tz0`): the ray enters through the YZ-plane (index 0). If `tym < tx0`, set bit 2: `entry |= 2`. If `tzm < tx0`, set bit 1: `entry |= 1` [S1, unofficial].
+   - Else if `ty0` is larger than `tz0`: the ray enters through the XZ-plane (index 1). If `txm < ty0`, set bit 2: `entry |= 4`. If `tzm < ty0`, set bit 1: `entry |= 1` [S1, unofficial].
+   - Else (`tz0` is largest): the ray enters through the XY-plane (index 2). If `txm < tz0`, set bit 2: `entry |= 4`. If `tym < tz0`, set bit 1: `entry |= 2` [S1, unofficial].
+3. Return `entry` [S1, unofficial].
+4. Compare exit parameters `tx1` and `ty1` [S1, unofficial].
+5. If `tx1 < ty1`, set `min_t = tx1` and `exit = 0` (YZ-plane) [S1, unofficial].
+6. Else, set `min_t = ty1` and `exit = 1` (XZ-plane) [S1, unofficial].
+7. If `tz1 < min_t`, set `exit = 2` (XY-plane) [S1, unofficial].
+8. Return `octantTable[currentOctant][exit]` [S1, unofficial].
 
